    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d71-a2">

                <pb facs="0132" n="82" sameAs="frus:frus1894/pg82"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No. 295.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Thompson to Mr. Nascimento.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Petropolis</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-09-25"><hi rendition="#italic">September 25,
                        1894</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt of the note which his excellency, Dr.
                    Cassiano do Nascimento, minister for foreign affairs, sent to me on the 22d
                    instant, containing information of the steps taken by his excellency the
                    vice-president with the view of terminating the commercial arrangement of
                    January 31, 1891.</p>
                <p>I avail, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Thos. L.
                    Thompson.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
